      "label": "lab experiment",
      "skos:prefLabel": "lab experiment",
      "description": "Lab Experiment refers to a research method involving controlled and systematic investigation conducted in a laboratory setting. It is used to test hypotheses, observe phenomena, and gather empirical data under controlled conditions. This property highlights that the research contribution includes experimental work carried out in a lab environment, emphasizing the empirical and reproducible nature of the study.",
