      "@type": "rdf:Property",
      "label": "security model",
      "skos:prefLabel": "security model",
      "description": "Security Model refers to the set of mechanisms and principles used to ensure the protection of systems, data, and interactions in LLM-tool integration environments. It encompasses authentication, authorization, isolation, and monitoring strategies that prevent unauthorized access, misuse, or adversarial exploitation. In the context of research, this property highlights how security is enforced within the proposed approach, such as introducing novel protection mechanisms, strengthening existing safeguards, or analyzing vulnerabilities related to tool usage.",
